20. The diagram shows the graph of $y = f'(x)$.
[Diagram: cubic-shaped curve $y = f'(x)$ with no scale, crossing the $x$-axis at a negative value, at the origin and at a positive value; local maximum between the first two roots and local minimum between the last two]
Indicate, and label clearly, on the graph
(a) the points where $y = f(x)$ has minimum points;
(b) the points where $y = f(x)$ has maximum points;
(c) the points where $y = f(x)$ has points of inflexion.
